{"i": "For {proj}, '{req}' sees duplicate rows appear when two users act at once. What database reasoning prevents it properly?",
 "a": "Reason about the isolation level and uniqueness enforcement: application-side checks race under concurrency, while constraints and upserts enforce uniqueness atomically in the database. Application locks do not span instances. Enforce at the layer that cannot be bypassed."},
